# Defect 016's group shape (panel 230's R2, M-panic-location step 10): an `assert`
# on two records of a header's wrote its expression and no side, until the sides were written as
# the specification writes the values, in the lldb formatter's notation and
# within its bounds. The line checked is the one that shows the shape.
# The fixed array is walked; the pointer and the C string are written as
# their address and never read through (the ffi-pragmatist's veto), the null
# one as `nullptr`. The address is the run's, so the line is checked up to it.

extern "fixedbugs-016-an-assert-on-a-group-record-writes-its-members-and-reads-no-address.h"
    record Pair
        id: i32
        pair: f32[2]
        raw: ptr
        name: cstr
    function pair_make(id: i32) -> Pair

function main()
    a = pair_make(id: 1)
    b = pair_make(id: 2)
    assert a == b
